  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "How to recreate:\nMake a gameobject and give it any component. Make another gameobject and give it an udon graph. Open the udon graph and drag in the first gameobject to make it a variable, then delete that variable. Then drag in one of its components, which makes a variable with the same name as the previous variable.\nCompile the graph and it appears fine. However, once you click back on the gameobject with your udon graph, it immediately breaks and gives the error \"Specified cast is not valid.\" The graph is now soft locked and nothing can fix it unless you restart unity or delete the graph and start over.",
